.TH CLAUDE-CAGE 1 "February 2026" "claude-cage 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-cage \- a sandboxed git workflow for Claude Code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-cage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-cage
creates an isolated sandbox for Claude Code using git-based file isolation.
It creates a sanitized copy of your project (excluding sensitive files) and
uses git to sync changes back to your source repository.
.PP
Key features:
.IP \(bu 2
No sudo required \- runs as current user
.IP \(bu 2
Git-based sync \- uses git archive + fresh init
.IP \(bu 2
File exclusion at archive time (no history of excluded files)
.IP \(bu 2
Network filtering via iptables (optional)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B git-merge
Fetch refs from intermediary repository for manual merge. Use this when
autoMerge is disabled and you want to bring Claude's changes back to source.
.TP
.B clean
Remove cached branch data. With no arguments, presents interactive selection.
Use \fB\-\-branch\fR to specify a branch directly.
.TP
.B clean-all
Remove all cached branches for the current project. Prompts for confirmation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-test
Drop into an interactive shell for testing instead of launching the
configured command.
.TP
.B \-\-direct-mount
Mount the source directory directly into the sandbox without git sync.
Changes made inside the sandbox immediately affect source files.
.TP
.B \-\-branch \fINAME\fR
Specify branch for the \fBclean\fR command. The branch name is automatically
sanitized for filesystem compatibility.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show commands without executing them. Useful for understanding what
claude-cage will do.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Show commands as they execute. Helpful for debugging.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Show full command output (implies \fB\-\-verbose\fR).
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version number and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are loaded and merged in order (later values override,
arrays merge):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
/etc/claude-cage.conf              System-wide
~/.config/claude-cage/config       User
<ancestors>/.claude-cage           Ancestor directories
.claude-cage                       Project (current directory)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Configuration uses Lua syntax:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude_cage {
    launch = "claude",
    mode = "bwrap",
    autoMerge = true,
    exclude = { ".env", "secrets/**" },
    networkMode = "allowlist",
    allow = {
        domains = { "github.com:443" }
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.SS Configuration Options
.TP
.B launch
Command to run inside sandbox (default: "claude")
.TP
.B mode
Sandbox mode: "bwrap" or "docker" (default: "bwrap")
.TP
.B autoMerge
Enable real-time sync via named pipe (default: false)
.TP
.B exclude
Array of patterns to exclude from archive
.TP
.B directMount
Mount source directly without git sync (default: false)
.TP
.B allowNonGit
Allow running in non-git directories (default: unset, prompts)
.TP
.B isolated
Only mount single project instead of all same-branch projects (default: false)
.TP
.B showBanner
Show ASCII banner on startup (default: true)
.TP
.B hideConfirmationPrompt
Skip the startup confirmation prompt (default: false)
.TP
.B createCagedDir
Create .caged/ symlinks to branch caches (default: false)
.TP
.B additionalMounts
Extra mounts for sandbox
.TP
.B networkMode
Network filtering: "disabled", "allowlist", or "blocklist" (default: "disabled")
.TP
.B allow
Allowed destinations when networkMode is "allowlist"
.TP
.B block
Blocked destinations when networkMode is "blocklist"
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CAGE_CACHE
Override cache directory (default: ~/.cache/claude-cage)
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CAGE_RUNTIME
Override runtime directory (default: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-cage)
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CAGE_BRANCH
Override branch name for path construction (auto-detected from source)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude-cage/branches/<branch>/work/
Clone of intermediary where Claude works
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude-cage/branches/<branch>/intermediary/
Sanitized repo (git origin for work)
.TP
.I ~/.cache/claude-cage/branches/<branch>/state-*
Last processed source commit ID
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-cage/pipes/
Named pipes for communication
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/claude-cage/sessions/
Session tracking (PID files)
.SH EXAMPLES
Start sandbox with configured launch command:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage
.fi
.RE
.PP
Drop into a shell for testing:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage --test
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pass arguments through to launch command:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage --resume
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean up cache for a specific branch:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage clean --branch main
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fetch intermediary refs for manual merge:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
claude-cage git-merge
.fi
.RE
.SH PLATFORM SUPPORT
.TP
.B Linux
Both bwrap and docker modes supported
.TP
.B Windows (WSL 2)
Both bwrap and docker modes supported
.TP
.B macOS
Docker mode only (bwrap requires Linux kernel features)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bwrap (1),
.BR docker (1),
.BR git (1)
